    "kind": "external",
    "url": "https://www.aoguide.app/guide/",
    "extraLinks": [],
    "access": "ok",
    "verified": "2026-10-23",
    "why": "\"The guide goes over pretty much all of the theoretical concepts needed for astronomy olympiads.\" Prerequisites: \"basic understanding of high school level mathematics and physics. Familiarity with calculus and basic mechanics is required.\" Units: Positional Astronomy (The Sphere · Coordinate Systems · Time · Perturbation in Astronomical Observations · Sun, Moon and Planets) · Photometry (Radiometry · Magnitude Systems · Radiation Mechanism · Detectors · Types of Telescopes) · Celestial Mechanics (Kepler's Laws · Bound Orbits · Unbound Orbits · Orbital Elements · Three Body Systems · Orbital Maneuvers · General Relativity) · Stellar Astrophysics (Stellar Structure · Classification · Binary Systems · Stellar Evolution · Solar System) · Galactic Astrophysics (Galaxies · The Milky Way) · Cosmology (Our Universe · Geometry of the Universe · The Friedmann Equations) · Practical Astronomy. Each unit has an \"Advanced Topics\" section and a Recommended Reading list.",
    "highlight": true,
    "origin": "external",
    "sourceIds": [
      "S1"
    ],
    "needsReview": false
  },
